rding to the initial number of polyps</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.001</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Miss rate of colorectal polyps according to polyp size</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.159</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Patient characteristics associated with recurrence</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>CI, confidence interval.</p><p><sup>*</sup>Family history of colorectal cancer in a parent or sibling</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Adenoma characteristics associated with recurrence</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>CI, confidence interval.</p><p><sup>*</sup>Adenomas in both the distal colon and rectum and proximal colon.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Multivariate logistic regression for adenoma recurrence</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>CI, confidence interval.</p><p><sup>*</sup>Adjusting for age, sex, and other adenoma characteristics.</p><p><sup>&#x02020;</sup>Adenomas in both the distal colon and rectum and proximal colon.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T6" position="float"><label>Table 6</label><caption><p>Adenoma characteristics at baseline and endpoint colonoscopy</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjim-24-196-i006"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.001 compared with baseline adenoma.</p><p><sup>&#x02020;</sup>Adenomas in both the distal colon and rectum and proximal colon.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap>